For papers in the current search results, we merge with any existing decision
data.
If the paper was previously reviewed, we preserve the decision status, tags,
and LLM metadata while using the fresh paper data from the search (which may
have updated abstracts or other fields from enrichment).

Since a paper can appear in multiple providers, we also deduplicate within the
current result set.
When we encounter a duplicate paper ID, we keep a single [[ReviewDecision]] and
merge the underlying [[Paper]] objects to consolidate metadata (e.g., a missing
abstract in one provider and a present abstract in another).

A session entry may also be an \emph{adopted preprint}
(\cref{preprint-module}): enrichment replaced the published paper with
its preprint, keeping the published DOI in [[published_versions]].
Adoption breaks the id-based matching in both directions, and each
direction needs its own guard:
\begin{description}
\item[Published returns after adoption] The session holds the adopted
  preprint; a re-run returns the published version under its old id,
  which matches no decision.  The provenance lookup below maps each
  recorded published DOI back to its adopted entry, so the returning
  published paper is folded into that entry (content gaps filled via
  [[merge_version_of]], which never disturbs the preprint's identity)
  instead of re-entering as a fresh pending paper.
\item[Adoption arrives after the published entry] The session holds
  the published entry from an earlier run; a re-run with enrichment
  now delivers the adopted preprint under a \emph{new} id.  Here the
  incoming paper itself carries the link: its [[published_versions]]
  DOI matches the existing decision, whose entry we upgrade to the
  preprint identity---preserving the decision status and tags, since
  the work under review is unchanged---and re-key.  The persistent
  note and decision stores are migrated the same way
  ([[migrate_paper_id]], \cref{notes-module}).
\end{description}

<<convert search results to decisions>>=
decision_lookup: dict[str, ReviewDecision] = {
    get_paper_id(d.paper): d for d in session.decisions
}
provenance_lookup: dict[str, ReviewDecision] = {}
for d in session.decisions:
    for entry in d.paper.published_versions or []:
        published_doi = entry.get("doi")
        if published_doi:
            key = f"doi:{Paper._normalize_doi(published_doi)}"
            provenance_lookup[key] = d

for result in results:
    for paper in result.papers:
        paper = _normalize_paper_identifiers(paper)
        paper_id = get_paper_id(paper)

        existing = decision_lookup.get(paper_id)
        if existing is not None:
            try:
                existing.paper = existing.paper.merge_with(paper)
            except ValueError:
                pass
            continue

        adopted = provenance_lookup.get(paper_id)
        if adopted is not None:
            adopted.paper = merge_version_of(adopted.paper, paper)
            continue

        replaced = None
        for entry in paper.published_versions or []:
            published_doi = entry.get("doi")
            if not published_doi:
                continue
            old_id = f"doi:{Paper._normalize_doi(published_doi)}"
            replaced = decision_lookup.get(old_id)
            if replaced is not None:
                break
        if replaced is not None:
            migrate_paper_id(get_paper_id(replaced.paper), paper_id)
            replaced.paper = merge_version_of(paper, replaced.paper)
            decision_lookup[paper_id] = replaced
            provenance_lookup[old_id] = replaced
            continue

        # Check for previous decision (prefer session data over notes)
        prev_dec = prev_decision_lookup.get(paper_id)
        prev_record = None
        if not prev_dec and previous_decisions:
            prev_record = previous_decisions.decisions.get(paper_id)

        # Backward compatibility: if the paper gained a DOI, the previous
        # decision may have been keyed by the legacy hash id.
        if (prev_dec is None or prev_record is None) and getattr(paper, "doi", None):
            legacy_id = legacy_hash_paper_id(paper.title, paper.authors)
            if prev_dec is None:
                prev_dec = prev_decision_lookup.get(legacy_id)
            if prev_record is None and previous_decisions:
                prev_record = previous_decisions.decisions.get(legacy_id)

        if prev_dec:
            # Use previous decision but with fresh paper data
            decision = ReviewDecision(
                paper=paper,  # Fresh paper data from search
                provider=result.provider,
                status=prev_dec.status,
                tags=prev_dec.tags,
                source=prev_dec.source,
                is_example=prev_dec.is_example,
                llm_confidence=prev_dec.llm_confidence,
            )
        elif prev_record:
            # Fallback to notes module format
            status = DecisionStatus.PENDING
            if prev_record.status == "kept":
                status = DecisionStatus.KEPT
            elif prev_record.status == "discarded":
                status = DecisionStatus.DISCARDED
            tags = extract_tags_from_record(prev_record)

            # Restore LLM fields from notes if available
            source = ReviewSource.HUMAN
            source_str = getattr(prev_record, "source", "human")
            try:
                source = ReviewSource(source_str)
            except ValueError:
                pass

            decision = ReviewDecision(
                paper=paper,
                provider=result.provider,
                status=status,
                tags=tags,
                source=source,
                is_example=getattr(prev_record, "is_example", False),
                llm_confidence=getattr(prev_record, "llm_confidence", None),
            )
        else:
            # New paper, no previous decision
            decision = ReviewDecision(
                paper=paper,
                provider=result.provider,
                status=DecisionStatus.PENDING,
            )

        session.decisions.append(decision)
        decision_lookup[paper_id] = decision
