\subsection{Citation keys for the report}

The report keeps its own key scheme, [[surname{year}_{index}]], and keys
the map by [[id(decision)]] rather than by paper id. Both are deliberate.
The index suffix makes keys unique by construction, which matters because
[[load_session]] can hand back two decisions that resolve to the same
paper id (it derives arXiv DOIs from URLs at load time, so two entries
that were distinct when saved may coincide afterwards); keying by object
identity keeps both, whereas a paper-id map would silently drop one and
biber would then reject the duplicate entry key. The scheme is not shared
with the synthesis because the synthesis caches LLM prose that contains
its keys literally; changing either scheme to match the other would make
cached prose cite keys that no longer exist.

<<review report generation>>=
def report_cite_keys(decisions: list[ReviewDecision]) -> dict[int, str]:
    """Map `id(decision)` to a unique citation key for each decision."""
    keys: dict[int, str] = {}
    for index, decision in enumerate(decisions):
        paper = decision.paper
        if paper.authors:
            first_author = paper.authors[0].split()[-1].lower()
            first_author = ''.join(c for c in first_author if c.isalnum())
        else:
            first_author = "unknown"
        year = paper.year or "nd"
        keys[id(decision)] = f"{first_author}{year}_{index}"
    return keys
@

Keying by object identity is what keeps two decisions for one paper
apart:

<<test functions>>=
class TestReportCiteKeys:
    def test_same_paper_twice_gets_distinct_keys(self):
        paper = Paper(title="Twice", authors=["Ann Smith"], year=2024)
        decisions = [
            ReviewDecision(paper=paper, provider="a",
                           status=DecisionStatus.KEPT),
            ReviewDecision(paper=paper, provider="b",
                           status=DecisionStatus.DISCARDED),
        ]
        keys = report_cite_keys(decisions)
        assert len(set(keys.values())) == 2
        assert keys[id(decisions[0])] == "smith2024_0"
