\subsection{BibTeX entries}

Every paper becomes an [[@article]] entry: the metadata we hold does not
distinguish entry types reliably, and biblatex renders an article with
missing fields gracefully. The formatter is shared with the synthesis,
which used to carry a byte-for-byte copy.

The venue is coerced to a string before escaping. Some DBLP proceedings
records carry a two-element venue list (series and volume title), which
survives into the session file; the escaper then died on the list after
the CSV had already been written, leaving a half-finished export. The
provider should normalise this at ingest, but the exporter must not be
the place where a stray list turns into a traceback.

<<review report generation>>=
def format_bibtex_entry(paper: Paper, cite_key: str) -> str:
    """Format a paper as a BibTeX entry under `cite_key`."""
    lines = [f"@article{{{cite_key},"]
    lines.append(f"  title = {{{escape_bibtex(paper.title)}}},")
    if paper.authors:
        authors = " and ".join(paper.authors)
        lines.append(f"  author = {{{escape_bibtex(authors)}}},")
    if paper.year:
        lines.append(f"  year = {{{paper.year}}},")
    venue = paper.venue
    if isinstance(venue, (list, tuple)):
        venue = "; ".join(str(v) for v in venue)
    if venue:
        lines.append(f"  journal = {{{escape_bibtex(venue)}}},")
    if paper.doi:
        lines.append(f"  doi = {{{paper.doi}}},")
    if paper.url:
        lines.append(f"  url = {{{paper.url}}},")
    lines.append("}")
    return "\n".join(lines)


def build_report_bibtex(
    decisions: list[ReviewDecision],
    cite_key: Callable[[ReviewDecision], str],
) -> str:
    """Build the BibTeX file contents for `decisions`."""
    return "\n\n".join(
        format_bibtex_entry(d.paper, cite_key(d)) for d in decisions
    )
@

