@dataclass
class AuditRow:
    """One row of the audit table: a unique paper and its reason."""

    title: str
    year: str
    providers: list[str]
    status: DecisionStatus
    reason: str
    order: int
@

Two facts about how decisions are recorded shape the cited rule. First,
[[sessions decide -t]] appends to a row's tags, so a human who keeps an
LLM-classified [[supports-claim]] paper under a theme leaves both tags
on it; looking only at the first tag would file the paper under the
category and count no cited rows at all. The rule therefore splits the
tags into category and theme tags and takes the theme from the latter.
Second, an LLM keep is a candidate, not a citation: only a decision a
human made (or reviewed) counts as cited, which is also what the
[[decision_source]] column of the CSV export says. An LLM-kept paper
without a category tag falls through to the unknown-tag case, where its
theme is shown verbatim with the confidence.

The confidence is shown only for decisions the LLM made and nobody has
reviewed yet: once a human confirms or changes a decision it is a human
decision, and the number would misrepresent it.

<<review report generation>>=
def audit_reason(
    decision: ReviewDecision,
    *,
    theme_names: dict[str, str],
    strings: dict[str, str],
) -> tuple[str, int]:
    """Return the reason label and sort order for `decision`."""
    if decision.status == DecisionStatus.PENDING:
        return strings["pending"], AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER
    category_tags = [t for t in decision.tags if t in AUDIT_CATEGORIES]
    theme_tags = [t for t in decision.tags if t not in AUDIT_CATEGORIES]
    human_decision = decision.source != ReviewSource.LLM_UNREVIEWED
    if (
        decision.status == DecisionStatus.KEPT
        and human_decision
        and (theme_tags or not decision.tags)
    ):
        label = f"\\emph{{{strings['cited']}}}"
        if theme_tags:
            theme = theme_tags[0]
            label += ": " + escape_latex(theme_names.get(theme, theme))
        return label, AUDIT_ORDER_CITED
    if category_tags:
        tag = category_tags[0]
        label, order = strings[tag], AUDIT_CATEGORIES[tag]
    else:
        tag = decision.tags[0] if decision.tags else ""
        label, order = escape_latex(tag or "?"), AUDIT_ORDER_OTHER
    if (
        decision.source == ReviewSource.LLM_UNREVIEWED
        and decision.llm_confidence is not None
    ):
        label += f" ({decision.llm_confidence:.2f})"
    return label, order
@

